1
00:00:00,540 --> 00:00:05,130
Hello everyone and welcome to EnglishPod.

2
00:00:05,400 --> 00:00:05,810
My name is Marco.

3
00:00:06,270 --> 00:00:10,510
My name is Catherine and today we've got a very special lesson for you all about time.

4
00:00:11,030 --> 00:00:11,510
That's right.

5
00:00:11,690 --> 00:00:20,890
We're going to concentrate a little bit on some specific points of grammar this time and we're going to talk about the morning routine, what you do in the mornings.

6
00:00:21,390 --> 00:00:23,750
Well, let's take a look first at the word routine.

7
00:00:24,230 --> 00:00:26,370
This is our vocabulary preview for today.

8
00:00:28,440 --> 00:00:30,240
Vocabulary preview.

9
00:00:30,240 --> 00:00:32,590
Alright so a routine or the morning routine.

10
00:00:32,960 --> 00:00:34,240
What is a routine?

11
00:00:34,240 --> 00:00:40,390
A routine is basically your habit for a certain period of time.

12
00:00:41,080 --> 00:00:45,790
So for example, your routine in the morning is what you do when you wake up.

13
00:00:46,640 --> 00:00:47,570
Get breakfast and go to work.

14
00:00:48,160 --> 00:00:50,650
You can also have an evening routine.

15
00:00:51,120 --> 00:00:53,550
It's what you always do before you go to bed.

16
00:00:54,520 --> 00:00:55,520
Exactly.

17
00:00:55,520 --> 00:01:00,310
Everyone has a routine, what they do in the mornings, maybe what you do at night before going to bed.

18
00:01:00,960 --> 00:01:03,360
So that's what we're going to talk about today.

19
00:01:03,360 --> 00:01:04,360
That's right.

20
00:01:04,360 --> 00:01:05,360
You can also have an exercise routine.

21
00:01:05,360 --> 00:01:06,700
So basically anything with steps.

22
00:01:06,880 --> 00:01:10,280
One, two, three, four, five, that you always do the same way.

23
00:01:10,600 --> 00:01:11,600
That's a routine.

24
00:01:11,600 --> 00:01:12,600
Exactly.

25
00:01:12,600 --> 00:01:13,600
Right.

26
00:01:13,600 --> 00:01:14,600
So that's what we're going to take a look at today.

27
00:01:14,600 --> 00:01:26,080
Let's actually jump right into our dialogue and listen to Stephanie's routine.

28
00:01:26,180 --> 00:01:27,640
Stephanie did you just get to school?

29
00:01:28,100 --> 00:01:30,400
But you were up and about when I left the dorm this morning.

30
00:01:30,900 --> 00:01:32,340
That was about an hour and a half ago.

31
00:01:32,720 --> 00:01:33,640
This happens all the time.

32
00:01:33,980 --> 00:01:35,880
Why do you always take so long to get ready in the mornings?

33
00:01:36,560 --> 00:01:37,160
It's a skill.

34
00:01:37,780 --> 00:01:38,500
What can I say?

35
00:01:39,280 --> 00:01:40,240
I don't know why.

36
00:01:40,600 --> 00:01:41,780
I just have a long routine.

37
00:01:42,260 --> 00:01:44,600
Please explain because it makes no sense to me.

38
00:01:45,020 --> 00:01:46,980
How can a girl's routine be so complicated?

39
00:01:47,740 --> 00:01:52,340
You get up, you shower, you get dressed, you brush your teeth, you're out the door.

40
00:01:53,080 --> 00:01:53,820
Half an hour tops.

41
00:01:54,460 --> 00:01:59,060
Jacob, you have the luxury of having a haircut that rarely needs styling.

42
00:01:59,700 --> 00:02:00,460
I don't.

43
00:02:00,760 --> 00:02:04,020
I have to set aside about an hour and a half to get ready in the mornings.

44
00:02:04,700 --> 00:02:07,180
Every day I wake up and head straight for the shower.

45
00:02:07,740 --> 00:02:09,580
Every second day I wash my hair.

46
00:02:09,960 --> 00:02:15,820
If it's a hair washing day, I frequently need to wash my hair twice because it gets really oily.

47
00:02:16,600 --> 00:02:19,640
Then, I usually put in a conditioner and have to rinse that out too.

48
00:02:20,080 --> 00:02:25,020
Because my hair is so long, I seldom manage to take a shower in under 20 minutes.

49
00:02:25,780 --> 00:02:30,000
Afterwards, I often put on a pot of coffee and get dressed while I wait for it to brew.

50
00:02:30,820 --> 00:02:32,740
I take a long time to get dressed in the morning.

51
00:02:33,390 --> 00:02:38,250
Every now and then I remember to choose my outfit the night before, but usually I do it in the morning.

52
00:02:39,070 --> 00:02:45,130
In all, getting dressed takes about half an hour, at which time my hair is now semi-dry so then I have to style my hair.

53
00:02:45,690 --> 00:02:49,650
From time to time I'll put my hair up, but oftentimes I blow dry it straight.

54
00:02:50,800 --> 00:02:57,000
And then, because of the texture of my hair, I regularly have to flat iron it to keep it from frizzing.

55
00:02:57,000 --> 00:02:58,230
That's another 20 minutes or so.

56
00:02:59,240 --> 00:03:00,830
After that, I have my daily makeup routine.

57
00:03:01,670 --> 00:03:07,270
True, I hardly ever see you without your hair done and your makeup on, even when you show up to class in sweatpants.

58
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:10,650
Tell me, how long does it take you to choose that outfit in the morning?

59
00:03:11,480 --> 00:03:11,790
Not funny.

60
00:03:13,480 --> 00:03:19,040
Alright, we're back.

61
00:03:19,040 --> 00:03:21,220
So obviously she has a very complicated routine.

62
00:03:21,420 --> 00:03:22,740
I don't know if all girls are like this.

63
00:03:22,960 --> 00:03:26,380
I'm not like this, but I think a lot of girls, and some guys are.

64
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:28,120
I don't want to be sexist here.

65
00:03:28,160 --> 00:03:34,680
I know some guys who take their time in the morning and are very, very particular about the way that they look.

66
00:03:34,680 --> 00:03:35,680
Really?

67
00:03:35,680 --> 00:03:36,680
Wow.

68
00:03:36,680 --> 00:03:39,800
So, obviously everyone has their morning routine in different ways.

69
00:03:39,800 --> 00:03:42,040
And it was interesting to see how she described it.

70
00:03:42,140 --> 00:03:44,500
So why don't we take a look at Language Takeaway.

71
00:03:46,940 --> 00:03:47,900
Language Takeaway.

72
00:03:49,230 --> 00:03:54,110
So today's Language Takeaway, like I said at the beginning of the podcast, is all about time.

73
00:03:54,450 --> 00:03:56,890
So we're going to look at some of these important time adverbs.

74
00:03:57,430 --> 00:03:57,930
That's right.

75
00:03:58,150 --> 00:03:59,750
These are called adverbs of frequency.

76
00:04:00,280 --> 00:04:04,040
And basically, they are telling us how we do things.

77
00:04:04,070 --> 00:04:06,990
If we do something all the time or if we never do something.

78
00:04:07,800 --> 00:04:09,080
Or everything in between.

79
00:04:09,080 --> 00:04:10,080
Exactly.

80
00:04:10,080 --> 00:04:14,600
So the first couple we have today are very, very common words.

81
00:04:14,610 --> 00:04:15,430
You're going to hear these a lot.

82
00:04:15,730 --> 00:04:16,630
The first one is frequently.

83
00:04:17,380 --> 00:04:18,260
Okay, frequently.

84
00:04:18,680 --> 00:04:24,320
So, if you do something frequently, consider it to be about 75% of the time.

85
00:04:24,320 --> 00:04:27,040
Maybe a little bit more, almost 85% of the time.

86
00:04:27,040 --> 00:04:28,040
Right.

87
00:04:28,040 --> 00:04:29,980
So it's not always, but it's very often.

88
00:04:30,680 --> 00:04:36,460
So for example, so I frequently forget to take my keys when I'm leaving the house, which is a very big problem.

89
00:04:36,680 --> 00:04:36,900
Exactly.

90
00:04:37,300 --> 00:04:40,800
So considering out of seven days, maybe you forget your keys five days.

91
00:04:41,520 --> 00:04:42,520
Not so good.

92
00:04:42,520 --> 00:04:43,520
All right.

93
00:04:43,520 --> 00:04:44,520
So that's frequently.

94
00:04:44,520 --> 00:04:47,760
Now let's move on to another one that's actually a lot less.

95
00:04:48,140 --> 00:04:49,120
We talk about seldom.

96
00:04:50,100 --> 00:04:53,260
Well, Marco has told me that he seldom forgets his keys.

97
00:04:53,940 --> 00:04:56,440
That means he almost always remembers them.

98
00:04:56,800 --> 00:04:57,000
Right.

99
00:04:57,400 --> 00:04:59,380
So seldom is a negative adverb.

100
00:04:59,540 --> 00:05:00,980
It's saying that almost never.

101
00:05:01,880 --> 00:05:02,160
Okay.

102
00:05:02,200 --> 00:05:06,480
So if I say, for example, I seldom go to the movies.

103
00:05:07,080 --> 00:05:08,080
That's too bad.

104
00:05:08,080 --> 00:05:09,080
I like the movies.

105
00:05:09,080 --> 00:05:10,080
Right.

106
00:05:10,080 --> 00:05:13,280
Well, that means that I maybe go to the movie theater once a month.

107
00:05:13,640 --> 00:05:13,880
Yeah.

108
00:05:13,980 --> 00:05:14,900
Not very often.

109
00:05:15,800 --> 00:05:16,180
Seldom.

110
00:05:16,640 --> 00:05:17,640
Not very often.

111
00:05:17,640 --> 00:05:18,640
Seldom.

112
00:05:18,640 --> 00:05:19,640
All right.

113
00:05:19,640 --> 00:05:22,480
Now going back to a positive adverb of frequency, we have often.

114
00:05:22,480 --> 00:05:24,860
You described frequently as very often.

115
00:05:25,520 --> 00:05:25,640
That's right.

116
00:05:26,520 --> 00:05:33,320
You can also say, I often forget my keys or it often rains in tropical places.

117
00:05:33,320 --> 00:05:34,860
This means this is a common thing.

118
00:05:35,160 --> 00:05:35,480
Exactly.

119
00:05:35,880 --> 00:05:40,200
So again, let's consider it to be about 70 to 80% of the time.

120
00:05:40,580 --> 00:05:45,040
Now with pronunciation, some people like to pronounce often, right?

121
00:05:45,260 --> 00:05:48,240
They kind of leave out the strong T sound.

122
00:05:48,560 --> 00:05:50,620
Well, other people say often.

123
00:05:50,620 --> 00:05:50,740
That's right.

124
00:05:51,620 --> 00:05:52,620
Both forms are correct, right?

125
00:05:52,620 --> 00:05:52,760
Yes, they're both correct.

126
00:05:53,620 --> 00:05:56,080
So you're safe using either of these.

127
00:05:56,640 --> 00:05:57,640
Right.

128
00:05:57,640 --> 00:05:58,640
Okay.

129
00:05:58,640 --> 00:06:01,020
And our third adverb of frequency, no, our fourth.

130
00:06:01,600 --> 00:06:06,380
And our fourth adverb of frequency is also a positive one and we say usually.

131
00:06:07,720 --> 00:06:11,540
Usually means this is something that you do pretty consistently.

132
00:06:12,420 --> 00:06:16,380
I usually brush my hair before I go to sleep.

133
00:06:16,680 --> 00:06:19,360
That means not always, but almost every day.

134
00:06:19,520 --> 00:06:20,520
Right.

135
00:06:20,520 --> 00:06:22,800
So let's consider out of seven days, you do it six times.

136
00:06:22,800 --> 00:06:23,800
Yeah.

137
00:06:23,800 --> 00:06:24,460
I usually do this.

138
00:06:24,800 --> 00:06:25,800
Okay.

139
00:06:25,800 --> 00:06:27,920
So usually is again, very, very common.

140
00:06:28,920 --> 00:06:35,480
And something in between maybe 60% of the time, 50% of the time we say regularly.

141
00:06:36,240 --> 00:06:40,140
Well, I think of the word regularly as being very closely related to regular.

142
00:06:40,600 --> 00:06:45,020
So basically if I have a schedule, I do the same thing every day.

143
00:06:45,580 --> 00:06:46,600
I do it regularly.

144
00:06:47,180 --> 00:06:49,200
But sometimes there's a special occasion.

145
00:06:49,480 --> 00:06:54,140
For example, I regularly run five kilometers after work when I go to the gym.

146
00:06:54,520 --> 00:06:57,080
But sometimes when I want to go out with my friends, I don't run.

147
00:06:57,360 --> 00:06:59,600
So it's not always, but it is pretty regular.

148
00:07:00,160 --> 00:07:01,160
Exactly.

149
00:07:01,160 --> 00:07:06,880
So regularly means you do it very often, but there are some exceptions.

150
00:07:07,020 --> 00:07:07,140
Okay.

151
00:07:07,880 --> 00:07:14,860
Now those are adverbs of frequency, but we have a couple of other phrases that are very similar so we want to take a look at those as well.

152
00:07:15,900 --> 00:07:21,080
Let's go back to the beginning of Stephanie's routine when she said that every day I wake up.

153
00:07:21,620 --> 00:07:22,180
Okay.

154
00:07:22,200 --> 00:07:25,860
So every day means 100% of the time every single day.

155
00:07:26,060 --> 00:07:27,440
Monday to Sunday.

156
00:07:27,840 --> 00:07:28,040
Exactly.

157
00:07:28,540 --> 00:07:30,780
So obviously you wake up every day.

158
00:07:31,020 --> 00:07:33,140
Or I brush my teeth twice every day.

159
00:07:33,620 --> 00:07:36,020
So that's 100% of the time.

160
00:07:36,960 --> 00:07:40,960
Now if we say every second day, what does that mean?

161
00:07:41,360 --> 00:07:47,320
That means Monday yes, Tuesday no, Wednesday yes, Thursday no, or any day.

162
00:07:47,660 --> 00:07:51,140
So basically she says I wash my hair every second day.

163
00:07:51,520 --> 00:07:55,960
That means one day I wash my hair, but the next day I don't.

164
00:07:55,960 --> 00:07:59,600
The day after that though, I wash it again.

165
00:07:59,600 --> 00:08:00,430
Every second day.

166
00:08:00,630 --> 00:08:00,810
Okay.

167
00:08:00,830 --> 00:08:05,410
So you can say every second day and I think you can also say every other day.

168
00:08:06,160 --> 00:08:06,650
Every other day.

169
00:08:07,160 --> 00:08:08,910
So every other day or every second day.

170
00:08:09,160 --> 00:08:11,010
He calls his mother every other day.

171
00:08:11,560 --> 00:08:11,750
Very good.

172
00:08:12,560 --> 00:08:13,560
Alright.

173
00:08:13,560 --> 00:08:18,430
And she also said that every now and then I remember to choose my outfit.

174
00:08:19,080 --> 00:08:19,500
Okay.

175
00:08:19,520 --> 00:08:20,120
Well, this one's interesting.

176
00:08:20,600 --> 00:08:21,420
This is not very frequent.

177
00:08:22,080 --> 00:08:24,380
This is basically saying sometimes.

178
00:08:25,020 --> 00:08:25,500
Sometimes.

179
00:08:26,300 --> 00:08:27,560
So now and then.

180
00:08:27,560 --> 00:08:31,200
Every now and then means I sometimes do it, I sometimes don't do it.

181
00:08:31,920 --> 00:08:36,080
Every now and then I really want to eat chocolate so I buy a candy bar.

182
00:08:36,440 --> 00:08:36,740
Okay.

183
00:08:36,780 --> 00:08:40,220
So basically you want to eat chocolate twice in a month.

184
00:08:40,540 --> 00:08:41,320
Yeah, not very often.

185
00:08:41,480 --> 00:08:42,140
Not very often.

186
00:08:42,680 --> 00:08:43,680
Okay.

187
00:08:43,680 --> 00:08:46,680
And another one that's very similar is from time to time.

188
00:08:47,600 --> 00:08:50,720
So Marco said that he doesn't go to the movies very frequently.

189
00:08:50,720 --> 00:08:52,380
So he goes from time to time.

190
00:08:52,620 --> 00:08:52,740
Right.

191
00:08:52,920 --> 00:08:58,800
So I can say I seldom go to the movies or I can say I like to go to the movies from time to time.

192
00:08:59,080 --> 00:08:59,600
That's right.

193
00:08:59,860 --> 00:09:02,000
Or this girl is describing her appearance.

194
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:04,340
She says from time to time I put my hair up.

195
00:09:04,720 --> 00:09:05,900
So that means most of the time.

196
00:09:06,380 --> 00:09:07,740
That means sometimes it's down.

197
00:09:08,060 --> 00:09:08,700
Sometimes it's up.

198
00:09:09,520 --> 00:09:10,520
Right.

199
00:09:10,520 --> 00:09:18,880
So as you can see there are many different ways of describing the frequency or how many times you do certain actions or your routine.

200
00:09:18,880 --> 00:09:21,440
So you can use this with a lot of things when you're describing.

201
00:09:22,200 --> 00:09:29,580
And we encourage you to try some of these new ones because a lot of English learners use the same time adverbs whenever they speak.

202
00:09:29,840 --> 00:09:32,980
So try and really use some of these and challenge yourself.

203
00:09:33,260 --> 00:09:33,500
Exactly.

204
00:09:34,520 --> 00:09:36,960
All right so that's all we have for language takeaway.

205
00:09:37,360 --> 00:09:41,920
Why don't we move on now to Fluency Builder.

206
00:09:41,920 --> 00:09:42,170
Fluency Builder.

207
00:09:44,280 --> 00:09:53,700
Okay so using some of these adverbs I could say I can say I regularly make a pot of coffee in the morning.

208
00:09:54,280 --> 00:09:55,280
Okay.

209
00:09:55,280 --> 00:09:56,260
So a pot of coffee.

210
00:09:56,480 --> 00:09:57,880
You regularly make a pot of coffee.

211
00:09:58,080 --> 00:09:59,660
That means you like to drink coffee every day.

212
00:09:59,940 --> 00:10:00,160
That's right.

213
00:10:00,460 --> 00:10:02,260
I always need my cup of coffee in the morning.

214
00:10:02,560 --> 00:10:04,720
So I usually make it first thing.

215
00:10:05,440 --> 00:10:06,430
So a pot of coffee.

216
00:10:07,120 --> 00:10:08,810
We know what a cup of coffee is.

217
00:10:09,320 --> 00:10:10,130
But a pot of coffee.

218
00:10:10,320 --> 00:10:10,730
What is a pot?

219
00:10:11,320 --> 00:10:17,050
A pot is basically the container that you use when you brew coffee when you make it.

220
00:10:17,560 --> 00:10:24,810
So you put the coffee beans in the machine and instead of having a cup underneath you have a bigger container that's a pot.

221
00:10:25,640 --> 00:10:27,230
You can also have a pot of tea.

222
00:10:27,720 --> 00:10:28,070
Exactly.

223
00:10:28,720 --> 00:10:29,090
It's many cups.

224
00:10:29,720 --> 00:10:30,630
Usually eight or ten cups.

225
00:10:31,120 --> 00:10:32,120
All right.

226
00:10:32,120 --> 00:10:33,120
So what is that verb?

227
00:10:33,130 --> 00:10:33,850
To brew coffee.

228
00:10:34,120 --> 00:10:38,040
I think it's a very nice kind of fancy way of saying making coffee.

229
00:10:38,480 --> 00:10:39,470
Brew a pot of coffee.

230
00:10:39,480 --> 00:10:41,120
I'm brewing some coffee.

231
00:10:41,120 --> 00:10:42,120
All right.

232
00:10:42,120 --> 00:10:52,330
So apart from coffee and all of these things, let's take a look at some of the specific phrases that she used when she was talking about her hair because I think her hair is very complicated.

233
00:10:52,870 --> 00:10:54,070
It is very complicated.

234
00:10:54,880 --> 00:10:56,400
Sometimes she washes her hair.

235
00:10:56,400 --> 00:10:57,450
Sometimes she doesn't wash her hair.

236
00:10:58,200 --> 00:11:00,600
Sometimes she blow dries it straight.

237
00:11:00,600 --> 00:11:05,280
Okay, so to blow dry means that you use a blow dryer.

238
00:11:05,280 --> 00:11:06,280
That's right.

239
00:11:06,280 --> 00:11:12,400
This is a machine that uses electricity to blow hot air on your hair so that your hair will dry quickly.

240
00:11:13,480 --> 00:11:15,860
But you can blow dry your hair in many ways.

241
00:11:16,440 --> 00:11:20,840
Some people have curly hair and they have special tools for making their hair curly.

242
00:11:20,840 --> 00:11:22,800
But she says she blow dries it straight.

243
00:11:23,440 --> 00:11:25,580
That means she makes it straight with hot air.

244
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:26,180
Right.

245
00:11:26,420 --> 00:11:32,540
So I think the way you do this is you take the blow dryer and a brush and you brush while you blow dry, right?

246
00:11:32,800 --> 00:11:33,800
Yep.

247
00:11:33,800 --> 00:11:34,800
Awesome.

248
00:11:34,800 --> 00:11:35,800
Making lines.

249
00:11:35,800 --> 00:11:37,960
See, I know a little bit about this even though I don't have long enough hair for this.

250
00:11:37,960 --> 00:11:38,620
No, I guess.

251
00:11:38,900 --> 00:11:42,880
Well, maybe you are secretly one of those guys who has a routine like this woman.

252
00:11:43,360 --> 00:11:48,600
I don't think I can take this much time in the shower and brushing my hair.

253
00:11:49,760 --> 00:11:54,760
But moving on, actually, I also know this next phrase, to flat iron your hair.

254
00:11:55,710 --> 00:11:58,550
Okay, so flat iron is a noun and a verb.

255
00:11:58,880 --> 00:12:03,320
So I use a flat iron or I can flat iron my hair.

256
00:12:03,320 --> 00:12:06,150
This is a tool that we use that's very, very hot.

257
00:12:06,840 --> 00:12:07,270
Think of an iron.

258
00:12:07,870 --> 00:12:15,890
It's very, very hot and it basically presses my hair and makes it very, very, very thin and flat and straight.

259
00:12:17,320 --> 00:12:21,330
So I think people that have straight hair don't need to really flat iron their hair.

260
00:12:21,520 --> 00:12:24,920
Nah, but if you have very curly hair, then you need it.

261
00:12:24,920 --> 00:12:25,690
So what's the difference?

262
00:12:26,180 --> 00:12:26,850
Give us the insight here.

263
00:12:27,180 --> 00:12:29,290
Why wouldn't you just blow dry it straight?

264
00:12:29,800 --> 00:12:31,680
Why do you need to flat iron it?

265
00:12:31,900 --> 00:12:34,720
Because a flat iron makes it more flat.

266
00:12:35,200 --> 00:12:41,280
It makes your hair stick together more and it's much, much, much hotter than a blow dryer.

267
00:12:41,280 --> 00:12:47,180
So I guess if you use a blow dryer, then you have puffy hair or like the next word that she described, frizzy hair.

268
00:12:47,760 --> 00:12:52,460
Okay, so the adjective to describe this kind of hair is frizzy.

269
00:12:52,760 --> 00:12:56,000
For example, when it's very rainy, my hair is frizzy.

270
00:12:56,520 --> 00:12:57,820
That means that it sticks out.

271
00:12:58,080 --> 00:13:02,120
It's very thick and not straight.

272
00:13:02,120 --> 00:13:03,970
It's not curly, but it's messy.

273
00:13:05,200 --> 00:13:06,200
It kind of inflates.

274
00:13:06,390 --> 00:13:06,770
That's right.

275
00:13:07,210 --> 00:13:08,130
It's like a little balloon.

276
00:13:09,270 --> 00:13:11,910
But the verb here is to frizz.

277
00:13:12,570 --> 00:13:13,930
So my hair is frizzing.

278
00:13:15,230 --> 00:13:18,070
And that means that it's getting like this, bigger or inflated.

279
00:13:18,550 --> 00:13:18,750
That's right.

280
00:13:19,640 --> 00:13:25,240
So girls who have this problem have it worse during very humid or rainy days.

281
00:13:25,240 --> 00:13:26,960
Not so bad when it's dry.

282
00:13:26,960 --> 00:13:30,630
Okay, so I actually have a little bit of frizzy hair.

283
00:13:30,920 --> 00:13:36,040
That's why I have to use some sort of hair gel or mousse.

284
00:13:36,150 --> 00:13:37,590
See, it's not because I'm vain.

285
00:13:37,880 --> 00:13:41,240
It's just because if I don't use this, I'll come in looking like a lion.

286
00:13:42,370 --> 00:13:45,210
I think I might have to insist that that happens sometime soon.

287
00:13:45,240 --> 00:13:48,120
We can take a picture and put it on our website, EnglishBot.com.

288
00:13:48,120 --> 00:13:48,390
For sure.

289
00:13:49,120 --> 00:13:56,120
All right, so why don't we go back and listen to the dialogue one last time.

290
00:13:56,120 --> 00:14:03,560
Stephanie, did you just get to school?

291
00:14:03,560 --> 00:14:05,670
But you were up and about when I left the dorm this morning.

292
00:14:06,360 --> 00:14:07,670
That was about an hour and a half ago.

293
00:14:08,080 --> 00:14:08,970
This happens all the time.

294
00:14:09,270 --> 00:14:11,190
Why do you always take so long to get ready in the mornings?

295
00:14:12,040 --> 00:14:13,200
It's a skill.

296
00:14:13,200 --> 00:14:14,880
What can I say?

297
00:14:14,880 --> 00:14:15,540
I don't know why.

298
00:14:15,920 --> 00:14:17,080
I just have a long routine.

299
00:14:17,580 --> 00:14:19,900
Please explain because it makes no sense to me.

300
00:14:20,340 --> 00:14:22,280
How can a girl's routine be so complicated?

301
00:14:23,060 --> 00:14:27,660
You get up, you shower, you get dressed, you brush your teeth, you're out the door.

302
00:14:28,380 --> 00:14:29,120
Half an hour tops.

303
00:14:29,820 --> 00:14:34,380
Jacob, you have the luxury of having a haircut that rarely needs styling.

304
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:35,760
I don't.

305
00:14:36,060 --> 00:14:39,340
I have to set aside about an hour and a half to get ready in the mornings.

306
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:42,500
Every day, I wake up and head straight for the shower.

307
00:14:43,050 --> 00:14:44,870
Every second day, I wash my hair.

308
00:14:45,270 --> 00:14:51,110
If it's a hair washing day, I frequently need to wash my hair twice because it gets really oily.

309
00:14:51,910 --> 00:14:54,930
Then, I usually put in a conditioner and have to rinse that out too.

310
00:14:55,390 --> 00:15:00,310
Because my hair is so long, I seldom manage to take a shower in under 20 minutes.

311
00:15:01,090 --> 00:15:05,290
Afterwards, I often put on a pot of coffee and get dressed while I wait for it to brew.

312
00:15:06,110 --> 00:15:08,050
I take a long time to get dressed in the morning.

313
00:15:08,650 --> 00:15:13,550
Every now and then, I remember to choose my outfit the night before, but usually, I do it in the morning.

314
00:15:14,390 --> 00:15:20,450
In all, getting dressed takes about half an hour, at which time my hair is now semi-dry, so then I have to style my hair.

315
00:15:21,030 --> 00:15:24,970
From time to time, I'll put my hair up, but oftentimes, I blow-dry it straight.

316
00:15:26,080 --> 00:15:32,280
And then, because of the texture of my hair, I regularly have to flat iron it to keep it from frizzing.

317
00:15:32,280 --> 00:15:33,530
That's another 20 minutes or so.

318
00:15:34,520 --> 00:15:36,130
After that, I have my daily makeup routine.

319
00:15:37,000 --> 00:15:37,380
True.

320
00:15:37,680 --> 00:15:42,580
I hardly ever see you without your hair done and your makeup on, even when you show up to class in sweatpants.

321
